  "text": {
    "work": "work",
    "card": "Seat one hinge pin, swing the retained leaf, then align and withdraw it.",
    "hinge_pin": "hinge pin practice",
    "pin_state": "Choose an offer matching whether the pin is seated or racked.",
    "aligned": "Align both leaves before inserting or withdrawing the pin.",
    "phase": "Choose the swing matching the current indexed angle.",
    "free_hand": "Put down an object so a hand is free for the fixed practice control.",
    "howto_practice": "Use the purple fixed practice control. The gold P rack holds one original pin; insert moves that same continuous shaft and head into three hollow knuckles, with the head shoulder seated on the upper blue knuckle. Blue F is fixed; green M moves in three indexed endpoints: aligned,45 and90 degrees against red fixed legends. Only the aligned leaves permit insertion or withdrawal. Independent C-shaped retainers capture both leaves while the pin is racked; the separate rack cradle supports its head. Insert, swing outward twice, return twice, then withdraw and reuse. This is an integral teaching jig: it creates no loose pin, output or custody transfer. Its indexed endpoints depict assembly, not continuous insertion or swing, forces, friction, structural restraint, security, real-door authority or engine collision/support changes."
